{:id "0018-play"
 :title "`bb play`: one command to talk with Scout locally"
 :lupa/deps #{"0013-e2e-smoke"}
 :lupa/area :dev
 :lupa/risk :low
 :goal "The founder can try Half Ahead with one command: `bb play` starts
        the Firestore and Auth emulators, seeds them, starts the worker with
        the real `claude` engine (or --engine mock), compiles and serves the
        app, and prints the URL. Ctrl-C stops everything it started. The
        README says how."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/dev/play.clj" "test/halfahead/dev/play_test.clj"
         "bb.edn" "README.md"]
 :design "halfahead.dev.play (Babashka), reusing halfahead.dev.serve, the
          seed, and the worker task — no copies of their logic:
            (-main & args) runs `npx firebase emulators:exec --only
            firestore,auth --project demo-halfahead \"bb play:inner <args>\"`
            (emulators:exec stops the emulators when the inner script ends).
            (inner! opts) compiles the app (npx shadow-cljs compile app),
            runs the seed, starts the worker as a child process with the
            chosen engine (default claude), starts the static server on
            port 8000 (or the first free port after it), prints
            'Half Ahead is at http://127.0.0.1:<port>/ — Ctrl-C to stop',
            and waits. A JVM shutdown hook stops the worker and the server
            by their own handles (never by name).
            (parse-args args) is pure: --engine mock|claude, --port n;
            unknown flags throw ex-info {:type :ha/bad-args}.
          bb.edn: tasks `play` and `play:inner`, documented.
          README.md: keep the founder's opening paragraph verbatim; add a
          short 'Try it' section (npm ci; bb play; open the URL; sign-in is
          automatic on the emulator as Ben; bb play --engine mock for no
          model calls; bb test; bb e2e) and a 'Read first' list pointing to
          PRODUCT.md, DESIGN.md, DECISIONS.md, docs/research/."
 :acceptance
 ["parse-args: defaults {:engine :claude :port 8000}; --engine mock and
   --port 9000 parsed; an unknown flag throws :ha/bad-args (tests)"
  "In this container, `bb play --engine mock` started in the background
   serves the page (curl the printed URL gets 200 with the app's HTML)
   within 90 s, and after it is stopped by its process handle no worker,
   server or emulator it started remains (show `ps` in the final message)"
  "README keeps the founder's paragraph unchanged and adds the sections"
  "`bb test` stays green"]
 :non-goals
 ["Do not edit src/halfahead outside dev/play.clj; no app changes"
  "Do not run `bb e2e` (fixed ports; another line may use them)"]
 :context ["src/halfahead/dev/e2e.clj" "src/halfahead/dev/serve.clj"
           "src/halfahead/dev/seed.clj" "bb.edn" "README.md" "firebase.json"]
 :budget-usd 8.0}
